<title>SOUTH AFRICA: RUGBY UNION-BRITISH LIONS BEAT WESTERN PROVINCE 38-21.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-BRITISH LIONS BEAT WESTERN PROVINCE 38-21.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-05-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The British Lions beat Western Province 38-21 (halftime 18-14) in their rugby union tour on Saturday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Western Province - Tries: Dick Muir (2), Robby Brink. Conversions: Percival Montgomery (3).</p>
<p>British Lions - Tries: John Bentley (2), Allan Tait, Ieuan Evans. Conversions: Tim Stimpson (3). Penalties: Stimpson (4).</p>
</text>
